WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.647
Nfs2root

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:03.274
A 12-year-old pre-auth

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:03.911
remote root

00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:06.686
A 12-year-old pre-authentication

00:00:06.604 --> 00:00:08.184
remote root vulnerability

00:00:07.996 --> 00:00:08.797
in the Linux

00:00:08.609 --> 00:00:10.082
kernel's NFS server

00:00:10.236 --> 00:00:14.493
tracked as CVE-2026-99362

00:00:14.632 --> 00:00:15.811
The NFS server

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:16.577
runs inside the

00:00:16.389 --> 00:00:17.556
kernel and parses

00:00:17.368 --> 00:00:18.676
network input before

00:00:18.488 --> 00:00:19.124
it knows who

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:19.572
you are

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:21.808
Since 2014

00:00:21.961 --> 00:00:22.987
the Linux kernel

00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:23.600
listening on it

00:00:23.412 --> 00:00:24.591
has let anyone

00:00:24.402 --> 00:00:25.098
who can reach

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:25.676
it write into

00:00:25.487 --> 00:00:26.784
kernel memory before

00:00:26.596 --> 00:00:27.362
logging in

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.175
A 12-year-old heap

00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:30.472
overflow in Linux's

00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:31.769
NFSv4 .

00:00:31.581 --> 00:00:32.725
1 server lets

00:00:32.536 --> 00:00:33.868
an unauthenticated

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.225
client on tcp

00:00:35.048 --> 00:00:37.088
/ 2049 corrupt

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.831
kernel memory

00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:39.372
Full story on

00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:40.079
the dashboard
